5G Networks Roll Out Across the U.S., But Widespread Availability Still Years Away

5G wireless networks are expected to deliver significantly faster speeds and enable a new generation of technology. The four major nationwide carriers – AT&T, Sprint, T-Mobile, and Verizon – are all developing and testing 5G network technology, but widespread availability remains some time off. AT&T deployed the first 5G mobile network in the U.S. in December.

AT&T initially activated its next-generation network in 12 cities: Jacksonville and Orlando, Florida; Atlanta, Georgia; Indianapolis, Indiana; Louisville and Raleigh, North Carolina; New Orleans, Louisiana; Charlotte and Oklahoma City, Oklahoma; Dallas, Houston, San Antonio, and Waco, Texas. The company plans to expand 5G service to at least nine additional cities this year, including Chicago, Illinois; Las Vegas, Nevada; Minneapolis, Minnesota; Los Angeles, California;
